<string name="debloat_title">Debloat</string><string name="debloat_search_hint">Search…</string><string name="debloat_no_matches">No matching presets or packages.</string><string name="debloat_disclaimer_title">Guide labels are guidance, not a guarantee</string><string name="debloat_disclaimer_short">Tested on Xiaomi Redmi Note 14 Global ROM. Labels are guidance only, not a guarantee. Snapshot first, restore available. You are responsible for the result.</string><string name="debloat_disclaimer_read_more">Tap to read the full disclaimer</string><string name="debloat_disclaimer">These labels and presets were tested on a Xiaomi Redmi Note 14 with the Global ROM. Other devices and ROM versions can behave differently, and a package marked Safe may still remove a feature you use. Every change is snapshotted first and can be restored from Snapshots. You choose what to change and you are responsible for the result.</string><string name="debloat_present">On this device: %1$d of %2$d</string><string name="debloat_not_present">Not on this device</string><string name="debloat_not_applicable">not applicable for this action</string><string name="debloat_hint_suspend">Suspend keeps the app installed but stops it from running. The lightest change.</string><string name="debloat_hint_remove">Remove for this user hides a system app for this user only. The APK stays on the system partition, and Restore brings it back. Only system apps can be removed here.</string><string name="debloat_hint_restore">Restore brings back a system package removed for user 0, regardless of which app removed it. It uses Android package state, not VOID snapshots.</string><string name="debloat_apply">Apply to %1$d selected</string><string name="debloat_confirm_body">%1$s will be applied to %2$d packages from %3$s, one at a time with read-back. A snapshot is saved first and every change can be restored from Snapshots.</string>
